#! ia 1.0

@spec publication-identity-screening
  meaning
    says "Defines bounded publisher-side screening of exact frozen text artifacts against an external operator-selected private-identity registry, with unavailable input never reported as pass."
  work
    title "Publisher identity screening"
    status draft
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    source "docs/kit-contract/SCREENING-SPEC.md"
    covers ["tools/check-identities.mjs", "tests/check-identities.test.mjs", "docs/kit-contract/SCREENING-SPEC.md", "docs/kit-contract/screening-review.md", "docs/kit-contract/screening-verification.md"]

@task publication-identity-screening
  meaning
    says "Implement and independently qualify the publisher-context identity screening prerequisite under marketplace issue 22. Committed red and review stages precede the local implementation; 69 screening controls and 18 baseline integrity controls pass. Public review remains pending; operator registry acceptance and exact-payload screening are retained separately in private publisher evidence. Keep semantic disclosure review, kit pack integration and common checker qualification separate. Follow-up issue 23 owns expanded I/O and format qualification."
  work
    title "Qualify publisher identity screening"
    status open
    milestone @milestone kit-contract-baseline
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    start "2026-11-06"
    source "docs/kit-contract/SCREENING-SPEC.md"

@task publication-screening-hardening
  meaning
    says "Deliver marketplace issue 23 under plan kit-contract-qualification: qualify descriptor-bound bounded reads and exact file identities, high-token-count performance, broader complete kit formats and packing-boundary integration before extending the controlled frozen-text profile. Retain committed failing behavioral tests and independent reviews. No automatic publication authority or merge."
  work
    title "Harden and integrate publisher screening"
    status open
    milestone @milestone kit-contract-baseline
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    start "2026-11-06"
    source "docs/kit-contract/SCREENING-SPEC.md"

@plan kit-contract-qualification
  meaning
    says "Independently establish public kit-contract expectations, then qualify their native representation and owned checker before release consumers can rely on them."
  work
    title "Kit contract qualification"
    status open
    source "docs/kit-contract/SPEC.md"

@milestone kit-contract-baseline
  meaning
    says "A complete public expectation baseline is independently reviewed, screened and frozen before lowering."
  work
    title "Kit contract expectation baseline"
    status open
    plan @plan kit-contract-qualification
    exit "All four contracts, fourteen requirements, 163 cases and normative contexts have retained identities and semantics, independent public review evidence and authorized publication screening."
    source "docs/kit-contract/SPEC.md"

@spec kit-contract-public-baseline
  meaning
    says "Preserves proposed public kit-contract expectation data and normative context with integrity tests, without claiming behavioral execution, native admission or release permission."
  work
    title "Public kit contract expectation baseline"
    status draft
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    source "docs/kit-contract/SPEC.md"
    covers ["docs/kit-contract/SPEC.md", "docs/kit-contract/expectations.json", "docs/kit-contract/context.md", "docs/kit-contract/review.md", "docs/kit-contract/verification.md", "tests/kit-contract-baseline.test.mjs"]

@task kit-contract-public-baseline
  meaning
    says "Prepare, independently review and screen the complete public expectation baseline under marketplace issue 21. The proposed artifacts retain four contracts, fourteen requirements and 163 cases; eighteen integrity tests pass after committed red and independent review. Adoption and freezing remain pending until independent public approval and authorized screening of the adopted head are available. Exposure for public review is a separate publisher assessment. This does not execute the behavioral cases or qualify the checker."
  work
    title "Qualify the public kit-contract expectation baseline"
    status open
    milestone @milestone kit-contract-baseline
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    start "2026-11-06"
    source "docs/kit-contract/SPEC.md"

@plan marketplace-public-launch
  meaning
    says "Take the public catalogue from its first local cut to a published, host-qualified repository."
  work
    title "Public catalogue launch"
    status open
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@milestone marketplace-published
  meaning
    says "The catalogue is on GitHub as inventarch/marketplace, installs from Git in Claude Code and Codex, and its gates pass in CI on all three systems."
  work
    title "Published and qualified"
    status open
    plan @plan marketplace-public-launch
    exit "The repository is pushed by the operator, CI passes on main, and the host smoke runs record a pass for Claude Code and Codex at exact versions."
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@task qualify-claude-code
  meaning
    says "Install ia@inventarch from GitHub in Claude Code at a named version, after removing the CLI-rendered registration, and exercise it with realistic prompts: the three entry points trigger, the session hook prints the bootstrap, the account offer appears once at startup and stays silent when suppressed, the governance probe fires in a governed repository with no governance kit, the IA door starts from .mcp.json and its tools answer as mcp__plugin_ia_ia__*, a compaction re-injects the task pin, a kit's handlers run and a pre block applies only with .ia/governance.json, and agents dispatch with only their allowlisted tools."
  work
    title "Qualify the catalogue in Claude Code"
    status open
    milestone @milestone marketplace-published
    owner "Unassigned"
    start "2026-10-30"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

