# The IA 3.6.0 migration (2026-11-08): two releases. Release N migrates on the 3.5.x pins; release N+1 moves to 3.6.0.

@plan cli-3-6-0-migration
  meaning
    says "Move the catalogue to @inventarch/cli 3.6.0 and its IA door in two releases. Release N moves users onto installed kits on the 3.5.x pins. Release N+1 moves the pins, the door and the re-cut kits to 3.6.0, released and qualified."
    answers "What work moves the catalogue onto IA 3.6.0?"
  work
    title "IA 3.6.0 migration"
    status open
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    start "2026-11-08"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"

@milestone cli-3-6-0-release-n
  meaning
    says "Release N, on the 3.5.x pins. kit.mjs bind refuses without --install, and the plugin's resolver and checks refuse a bound kit the lock does not install. The session start names bound kits the lock does not install. The docs lead with the @inventarch/public-kits package. The catalogue's own lanes install locally. The kits are re-cut on CLI 3.5.0 with their new guidance."
    answers "When can users install their kits before any door enforces it?"
  work
    title "Release N: the migration on 3.5.x"
    status closed
    ended "2026-11-08"
    plan @plan cli-3-6-0-migration
    exit "Release N is tagged ia-v<version> by the operator's release pull request, and @inventarch/public-kits is published at its claimed version. A test repository that binds the kits and installs them by the documented package route returns packets from both door 3.5.x and door 3.6.0. kit.mjs bind and resolve.mjs refuse IA-CORE-KIT-NOT-INSTALLED for a bound kit that is not installed. The catalogue's own lanes resolve after its contributor setup. The host gates pass."
    source "docs/roadmap.md"
  relationships
    requires @decision public-cli-3-6-0-door-pin

@milestone cli-3-6-0-sources
  meaning
    says "The release N+1 sources pull request is merged, with the 3.6.0 pins and cohort, the hand-off guard, the closure default workspace, the kits' toolchain strings and the release note."
    answers "When are the 3.6.0 sources on main?"
  work
    title "Release N+1: 3.6.0 sources merged"
    status closed
    ended "2026-11-09"
    plan @plan cli-3-6-0-migration
    exit "The sources pull request is merged into main with a merge commit. Every CI gate passes except the consistency refusal for the kits' packing CLI, which only the stamp commit clears and which the pull request names."
    source "docs/roadmap.md"
  relationships
    requires @milestone cli-3-6-0-release-n
    requires @decision public-cli-3-6-0

@milestone cli-3-6-0-released
  meaning
    says "Release N+1 is out: the kits are re-cut on 3.6.0, the plugin is released, @inventarch/public-kits is published, and the catalogue is qualified on its hosts and on the three operating systems."
    answers "When is the catalogue released and qualified on 3.6.0?"
  work
    title "Release N+1: 3.6.0 released and qualified"
    status open
    plan @plan cli-3-6-0-migration
    exit "consistency.py passes on main after the 3.6.0 stamp. The operator's release pull request is merged and ia-v<version> is tagged. @inventarch/public-kits is published at the version packages/public-kits/package.json claims. The native qualification shards pass on Ubuntu, Windows and macOS, with their reports kept. claude plugin validate --strict and the Codex smoke pass and are recorded."
    source "docs/roadmap.md"
  relationships
    requires @milestone cli-3-6-0-sources
    requires @task native-qualification-refresh

@task cli-3-6-0-record-decisions
  meaning
    says "Lower the migration's decisions and these work records into .ia/src/decisions.ia and .ia/src/work.ia, and add each decision's row to docs/decisions.md and the plan's rows to docs/roadmap.md. Add public-cli-3-6-0, made by the operator; the pins task adds its supersedes of public-cli-3-5-0 at release N+1. Retarget task native-qualification-refresh to 3.6.0, and supersede or amend public-kit-lookup to say that a bound key needs the lock to install its kit."
    answers "Where do the migration's decisions and tasks enter the catalogue's records?"
  work
    title "Record the 3.6.0 decisions and tasks"
    status closed
    ended "2026-11-08"
    milestone @milestone cli-3-6-0-release-n
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    action "Add the records and their rows, then run python tools/validate.py and node tools/check-language.mjs."
    expected-artifact ".ia/src/decisions.ia, .ia/src/work.ia, docs/decisions.md, docs/roadmap.md"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"
  relationships

@task cli-3-6-0-install-migration
  meaning
    says "Move users onto installed kits on the 3.5.x pins. kit.mjs bind refuses IA-CORE-KIT-NOT-INSTALLED and writes nothing when the lock does not install the kit, unless --install is passed. --install and the refusal's remedy use the package route: seed a language-only lock when the workspace has none, then ia install --package @inventarch/public-kits@<v>, and use kit.mjs add only for a kit the package does not carry. The session start names bound kits the lock does not install, with that remedy. installedKits and installedKit read kind package entries. The refusal tables in ia:init and the three lanes gain IA-CORE-KIT-NOT-INSTALLED. The README quick start, the init steps, the lane remedies, SUPPORT.md and docs/public-kits-package.md lead with the package route."
    answers "How does the plugin move users onto installed kits before the door enforces it?"
  work
    title "Migrate users to installed kits (package route)"
    status closed
    ended "2026-11-08"
    milestone @milestone cli-3-6-0-release-n
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    action "Change lib/kit-ops.mjs bindOp, scripts/bootstrap.mjs, lib/kit.mjs installedKits and installedKit, and every doc and skill that names the bind-only route: the init and lane skills, the doctor skill, plugins/ia/README.md, README.md and SUPPORT.md. Seed the language lock from a bundled kit's lock filtered to inventarch/language, as tools/check-language.mjs does. Update tests/bootstrap.test.mjs and kit-authoring.test.mjs. Add a test that runs the real doors 3.5.0 and 3.6.0 against a repository that binds a kit, before and after the remedy."
    expected-artifact "plugins/ia/scripts/lib/kit-ops.mjs, plugins/ia/scripts/bootstrap.mjs, plugins/ia/skills/*/SKILL.md, README.md"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"
  relationships
    requires @decision public-cli-3-6-0-bind
    requires @decision public-cli-3-6-0-install-route

@task cli-3-6-0-own-lock
  meaning
    says "Keep the catalogue's lock ignored, and make the contributor setup run kit.mjs add <kit> . --apply for the three kits through npm run kits:install (public-cli-3-6-0-own-lock B). Add vendor/ia/ to .gitignore and to tools/consistency.py's ignored paths, and say how in CONTRIBUTING.md and AGENTS.md."
    answers "How do contributors' lanes in this repository satisfy the door?"
  work
    title "Install the catalogue's own kits locally"
    status closed
    ended "2026-11-08"
    milestone @milestone cli-3-6-0-release-n
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    action "After the setup, call ia_method for delivery.design at the repository root through door 3.6.0 and keep the packet, which shows no IA-CORE-KIT-NOT-INSTALLED."
    expected-artifact "CONTRIBUTING.md, .gitignore"
    source "docs/roadmap.md"
  relationships
    requires @decision public-cli-3-6-0-own-lock

@task cli-3-6-0-kit-guidance
  meaning
    says "Change the kits' install guidance to the package route. That covers ia-authoring's install-and-bind convention and ia-authoring-record's installed-kits convention, ia-kb's IA-CORE-NO-METHOD playbook, and ia-method's README. Edit kits/<kit>, then run node tools/bundle-kits.mjs --write."
    answers "What do the kits say about installing a kit in release N?"
  work
    title "Change the kits' install guidance"
    status closed
    ended "2026-11-08"
    milestone @milestone cli-3-6-0-release-n
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    expected-artifact "kits/ia-authoring, kits/ia-kb, kits/ia-method"
    source "kits/README.md"
  relationships
    requires @task cli-3-6-0-install-migration

@task cli-3-6-0-release-notes-n
  meaning
    says "Write release N's notes with node tools/release.mjs note --bump minor, so that release N is 1.4.0 (public-cli-3-6-0-release-n-bump B). Tell users to run the package route now, because the next release's door refuses a bound kit the lock does not install."
    answers "What do release N's notes say?"
  work
    title "Release notes for release N"
    status closed
    ended "2026-11-08"
    milestone @milestone cli-3-6-0-release-n
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    expected-artifact "releases/pending/*.json"
    source "releases/README.md"
  relationships
    requires @decision public-cli-3-6-0-release-n-bump
    requires @task cli-3-6-0-install-migration

@task cli-3-6-0-kit-stamp-n
  meaning
    says "Stamp release N's re-cut as patches on CLI 3.5.0, each on its kit's latest release (public-cli-3-6-0-kit-level; expected ia-method 0.7.3, ia-kb 0.9.3, ia-authoring 0.1.3). Set source.commit, pack each kit, then run bundle, index and package --write. Raise packages/public-kits/package.json, and merge with a merge commit."
    answers "How are the kits re-cut for release N?"
  work
    title "Re-cut the kits for release N"
    status closed
    ended "2026-11-08"
    milestone @milestone cli-3-6-0-release-n
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    expected-artifact "kits/*/releases/<version>.json, kits/index.json, packages/public-kits/package.json"
    source "kits/README.md"
  relationships
    requires @task cli-3-6-0-kit-guidance
    requires @decision public-cli-3-6-0-kit-level

@task cli-3-6-0-host-gates-n
  meaning
    says "Run claude plugin validate --strict plugins/ia and claude plugin validate --strict ., then node tools/smoke-codex.mjs against a real Codex executable, for release N. Commit the smoke report."
    answers "Do the hosts accept release N?"
  work
    title "Host gates for release N"
    status closed
    ended "2026-11-08"
    milestone @milestone cli-3-6-0-release-n
    owner "InventArch maintainers"
    expected-artifact "the Codex smoke report"
    source "AGENTS.md"
  relationships
    requires @task cli-3-6-0-kit-stamp-n

@task cli-3-6-0-release-n
  meaning
    says "The operator dispatches .github/workflows/release-pr.yml and merges the release pull request it opens, which tags ia-v<version>. The operator then dispatches .github/workflows/publish-public-kits.yml, so that the package the docs name exists. The package version in plugins/ia/config/public-kits.json is published, which npm view @inventarch/public-kits@<that version> shows, before the release pull request merges: the plugin's install route fails until it is."
    answers "How is release N released and the public kits published?"
  work
    title "Release N and publish the kits"
    status closed
    ended "2026-11-08"
    milestone @milestone cli-3-6-0-release-n
    owner "Operator"
    action "Done: the operator merged the release pull request (#30), which tagged ia-v1.4.0 at 8f32d9fb, and published the package: npm view @inventarch/public-kits versions lists 1.0.3. A repository that installed the kits by the package route returned packets from door 3.5.x and door 3.6.0, the catalogue lanes resolved and the host gates passed (the description of pull request #29)."
    expected-artifact "tag ia-v<version>; @inventarch/public-kits on npm"
    source "releases/README.md"
  relationships
    requires @task cli-3-6-0-host-gates-n
    requires @task cli-3-6-0-release-notes-n

@task cli-3-6-0-pins
  meaning
    says "Move every pin to 3.6.0. That covers package.json and package-lock.json; the released block of sources.lock.json (cli, cliNpmIntegrity, and sourceCommit 63f18449a17e102d74200fc6e62e60e9c5222f1d); lib/cli.mjs PINNED, which is also the door's pin; closure-runtime.mjs and method-closure.mjs; qualified-runtime-3.6.0.json, regenerated by tools/qualify-runtime-cohort.py; run-native-tests.mjs, verify-native.mjs and validate.py; export-selection.json; and the version strings in the docs and tests."
    answers "Which files move to the 3.6.0 pins?"
  work
